course: dictionary
lesson: 13404
title: Hereditary: passed down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hereditary is a long word, but the sentence around it gives you clues. Look for what is passed on and who it is passed from. «Eye colour is hereditary, so Mia has her mum's brown eyes.» The words passed from her mum tell you that hereditary means handed down from parents to children.
explain: The same idea works for titles and jobs. «The hereditary king's eldest son will one day wear the crown.» The crown goes down the family line from parent to child, not because someone won it. Ask yourself: what is passed down? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Hereditary means passed from parents to children.
fact: In science, a hereditary feature or illness comes through genes, such as eye colour or freckles.
fact: In history and politics, a hereditary title, job or right is passed down in a family, like a crown.
fact: «Hereditary monarchy» means a country where the king or queen comes from one royal family by birth.
exercise: «Freckles are hereditary, so they often run in families.» What does hereditary mean here? | Caused by too much sun | Painful to touch | *Passed from parents to children | Only found on faces
exercise: «Some illnesses are hereditary.» Ben says hereditary means you catch it from a friend at school. What does it really mean? | Very dangerous and fast | Caught from a friend at school | *Passed from parents to children through genes | Something that makes you sneeze
exercise: «The hereditary title goes to the eldest son.» Which word tells you the title is passed down in a family? | goes | eldest | *hereditary | title
test: «The crown is hereditary.» Which clue shows this? | It is made of gold | *It passes from parent to child in the royal family | It is worn on special days | It is very old and heavy
test: Which sentence uses hereditary correctly? | I ate a hereditary sandwich | *Her hereditary illness runs in her family | She hereditary the cake | The hereditary bus was late
exam: What does hereditary mean? | Made of metal | Finished quickly | Given by a teacher for a good test | *Passed down in a family from parent to child
